# Maven build output
target/
!**/src/main/**/target/
!**/src/test/**/target/
HELP.md
.flattened-pom.xml

# Maven wrapper (only-script): keep mvnw / mvnw.cmd / maven-wrapper.properties;
# the downloaded distribution lives under ~/.m2/wrapper and is never committed.

# SSO-3088 → SSO-3715 / SSO-3717 — provisioning receipts. Since cli-v0.36.0 (SSO-3715; oauthy ADR
# 2026-10-15-platform-is-the-ledger-no-committed-provisioning-receipt) the engine writes NO receipt: `plan`, `apply`,
# `destroy` and `import` read live state only, and the platform's `owner` relation is the ledger of what a repository
# may remove. An older CLI (≤ cli-v0.34.x) still writes `<name>.receipt.json` next to the file, so the pattern stays
# one release to keep such a file out of a commit. Every receipt is ignored — SSO-3697's `!.thoryn/provision.receipt.json`
# exception is gone with the receipt pull request it served (SSO-3717): nothing is committed back by the apply job.
.thoryn/*.receipt.json

# SSO-3119 — `--secret-file` output. `provision apply` / `clients create` write a one-time client
# secret to the path you name, and the natural place to type is the repo you are standing in. A
# credential must never reach a commit, so the extension is ignored outright.
*.secret

